# UI design standard

Before changing any screen, style, or component, read `DESIGN.md` and follow it for the code you touch.

- Colors only from tokens (`--lvt-*` in `src/styles.css`; module aliases must point to them; homeroom status uses `--hr-*`). No new hex values in page CSS.
- Montserrat only; user-readable text ≥ 12px, body/inputs 14px.
- One primary action per area; destructive actions need confirmation.
- Labels above inputs, errors next to the field, never placeholder-as-label.
- Every screen has loading, empty, and error states; check 360px and 1280px widths.
- Changing the standard itself means editing `DESIGN.md` in the same PR.
